  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "There were initially XXX million people in a town, out of which YYY million people left the town and ZZZ million people immigrated to this town.\n\nDetermine the final population of town in millions.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case consists of three integers XXX, YYY and ZZZ.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output the final population of the town in millions.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤X,Y,Z≤101 \\leq X, Y, Z \\leq 101≤X,Y,Z≤10",
      "Y≤XY \\leq XY≤X"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n3 1 2\n2 2 2\n4 1 8\n10 1 10",
        "output": "4\n2\n11\n19",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The initial population of the town was 333 million, out of which 111 million people left and 222 million people entered the town. So, final population =3−1+2=4= 3 - 1 + 2 = 4=3−1+2=4 million.\nTest case 222: The initial population of the town was 222 million, out of which 222 million left and 222 million immigrated. The final population is thus 2+2−2=22+2-2 = 22+2−2=2 million."
      }
    ]
  },
